y the tool supports multiple questions. I'll do 2.\n\nI must also be careful: don't be sycophantic. Point out the double-count and the nominal branch-rate, and that the journal's percentage isn't trustworthy.\n\nLet me also mention the observation about `if(NOT CMAKE_*_FLAGS_COVERAGE)` guard: since flags are set in cache, `if(NOT ...)` compares the cache value; not a bug. But note: if a user passes `-DCMAKE_C_FLAGS_COVERAGE=\"/foo\"` the default won't apply — intended.\n\nAnother real defect to flag: `configure_target` for Coverage config: for MSVC, `target_link_options` Release-only adds /OPT:REF /OPT:ICF, so Coverage gets no /OPT — fine. But for GCC branch (`else()`), Coverage gets neither `-O2` nor `-g`, since both are under Debug/Release genexes. On Linux coverage is blocked by FATAL_ERROR, so fine today — but if Linux coverage is added, `CMAKE_C_FLAGS_COVERAGE` isn't defined for GCC (it'd be MSVC-style strings `/O2 /Ob1 /Zi`!). Wait — the CMAKE_*_FLAGS_COVERAGE block is unconditional (not inside `if(MSVC)`), so on Linux with a Coverage build you'd pass `/O2 /Ob1 /Zi /DNDEBUG` to g++ → breakage. Currently guarded by the FATAL_ERROR for non-Windows, so not reachable. Still worth noting as a latent trap for the \"coverage on Linux\" TODO (from journal: \"для его покрытия буду делать после\"). That's a good catch, [ФАКТ, ВЫСОКИЙ].\n\nHmm, actually is it reachable? `if(CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE STREQUAL \"Coverage\")` → else → FATAL_ERROR before configure. So unreachable now. Good — call it \"мина на будущее\".\n\nLet me write the response now. Keep it structured, not too long. Then the question tool.\n\nOne more: the user may just want to chat about coverage concepts. My question covers that.\n\nLet me write.",
