n. Options: print per-module lines, or aggregate product modules (needs parsing), or label it.\nC. Agreed change \"report then fail\" still not implemented (lines 32-34) — pending.\n\nNits:\n- `_line_rate` reused for block metric; misleading name/comment.\n- trailing space line 59.\n\nAlso: is there a check that `_xml` isn't stale? Covered by A.\n\nCould also suggest that since both merges are from the same raw, a failure of the second merge after the first succeeded should still fail — it does.\n\nOne more potential: `file(REMOVE)` list — should also remove `coverage.coverage`? yes it does.\n\nLet me also verify whether the native xml has `<module>` for each loaded module in a full run — can't without running. Fine.\n\nHow to verify B? We can inspect the existing native_t1_c.xml: only one module. So the flaw is theoretical for t1 but certain for full run (t1_cpp, t2, t3, t4, unit exes, shared DLLs → many modules). [ФАКТ, ВЫСОКИЙ that multiple modules will be present; the first one is arbitrary.]\n\nLet me check what's the first module in unit.cobertura? Not native. We only have one native xml. Fine.\n\nMaybe also check: in native xml, does `<module>` carry the exe path? `path=\"main.exe\"` — just the file name, not full path. So label would be ambiguous for 8 main.exe. Hmm. But block metric per module — you could show module id (GUID) which is meaningless. So the honest option: don't print a single \"block coverage\"; print per-module name (with duplicates) or skip for now.\n\nGiven the user asked \"check for errors\", I should give a concise review with severity ordering, and no edits (plan mode).\n\nLet me also double check whether `string(REGEX MATCH)` on a 400 MB file is fine — coverage.xml for full run may be larger (maybe 1-10 MB). `file(READ)` whole file then regex: fine, but on a big file it's a few MB. OK. Actually with 600 tests instrumented, the native xml could be tens of MB. Hmm: raw coverage was 410 KB for a handful of binaries; full run maybe several MB. `file(READ)` loads it fully — acceptable. But note: the regex engine on a multi-MB single string is fine (linear-ish). Not an issue.\n\nOne more: `file(READ)` on binary? no, xml is text.\n\nNow write the review concisely. Format: \"Функциональных ошибок нет / есть 2 + 1 незакрытое\". Use categories.\n\nAlso should I mention that `coverage.xml` removal matters also because the check `if(NOT EXISTS \"${_xml}\")` would pass on stale file — yes, combine.\n\nLet me present:\n\n**Ошибки (2)**\n1. `coverage.xml` не удаляется на старте (строки 12-13). Сценарий: предыдущий прогон дал отчёт; новый `collect` упал или `merge -f xml` упал → в `reports/` лежит старый `coverage.xml`, а проверка `EXISTS` на строке 61 его \"подтверждает\". И это ровно тот файл, по которому пойдёт анализ. Fix: добавить в file(REMOVE).\n2. \"block coverage\" = первый `<module>` в файле (строка 73). В полном прогоне модулей будет много (8 main.exe + common_*_shared.dll + unit exes), и печатается один произвольный. Плюс имя модуля не выводится → цифра не интерпретируема. Варианты: печатать `<module name>` рядом; или печатать по всем продуктовым модулям; или убрать до появления агрегатора.\n\n**Незакрытое из договорённого**\n3. Строки 32-34: при красном тесте по-прежнему FATAL до merge → ни cobertura, ни xml. Договорились: отчёт, потом падение.\n\n**Мелочи**\n- `_line_rate` используется для block-метрики (73) и комментарий (71) говорит \"line-rate\" — переименовать `_block_coverage`/поправить комментарий.\n- `endif() ` строка 59 — хвостовой пробел.\n- `coverage.xml` имя общее с \"какой-то xml\" — норм.\n\nAlso maybe: `file(REMOVE)` also could clear `logs/`? Not necessary.\n\nVerification: I haven't run the target (plan mode, no writes). So status: \"не проверено\" for runtime. I can truthfully say I only read.\n\nI should also note: `string(REGEX MATCH ... block_coverage=...)` picks the first module — and `<module>` order in the report may not be stable; can't verify without a multi-module run.\n\nKeep it concise. Then ask whether to include fixes in plan / whether they want the plan updated. Actually the user is in plan mode and asked to check. I'll give review + propose concrete fixes; ask if apply later (execution).\n\nLet me write.",
