n the new finding (union 96.4% vs 39.4%) and the 'main' package artifact, and what it means for the plan (summary exe now clearly justified; block metric not viable for main.exe group).\n\nLet me structure:\n\n1. FAILED = ninja's report that the custom target's command exited 1 (CMake script FATAL). Not a build failure. Quote lines.\n\n2. 5.1 verdict: all checklist items pass:\n   - 587 tests (=591−1−3, confirms exclusions)\n   - 1 failed (the broken one)\n   - raw 5.9MB, cobertura 347KB, native 3.2MB, fresh 12:07:55\n   - FATAL with both paths\n   - exit code: can't see (redirect swallowed $LASTEXITCODE); ninja `[code=1]` is printed in the FAILED line — actually that's the exit code of the custom command = 1. So exit code confirmed as 1. Good: `FAILED: [code=1]` is ninja's notation of the failed command's code.\n   - logs dir empty → `-l` with directory path ineffective.\n\n3. Step 5.3 answer (dedup): duplicates are real. 14 class entries for string_utils.cpp across modules. Union 96.4% vs root 39.4%. So the root metric must not be used as \"project coverage\"; and the summary exe is now justified (not speculative).\n\n4. New finding: native block metrics for `main` module are broken (0/0 blocks) because all 8 exes share OUTPUT_NAME main; the tool merges same-named modules into one package. So block_coverage cannot be used for tasks without renaming outputs. For DLLs it's fine.\n\n5. What's next:\n   - Preserve red-run evidence (copy reports + log) before the green run? The log `cvg_log.txt` persists (build/ ignored). Reports will be overwritten by the green run. Copy now (at execution time) to `build/coverage/probe/red-full/`.\n   - Revert the break.\n   - Reconfigure? The break is in a test source; `DEPENDS all` rebuilds. Then green full run.\n   - Then the union analysis becomes the basis for the summary tool.\n\n6. Also flag: the empty `logs/` — decide: change `-l` to a file path or remove the option.\n\nAlso: expected number of tests 587 — confirmed exactly. G