          "text": "Confirmed: all 38 functions of the merged `main` package have `blocks_covered=0, blocks_not_covered=0` — the block data is **zeroed** for the merged package, while line data survives. So it's not \"identical names → no branch metric\"; it's \"identical module names → block counters lost\". Line coverage for main is fine (75.90).\n\nSo:\n- Branch: absent in all formats (independent of names).\n- Block: present per module/function, but for the 8 task exes it's destroyed by the merge. Renaming OUTPUT_NAME would restore per-task block data.\n\nWould renaming be worth it? Let's weigh:\n\nPros:\n- block metrics for each of 8 tasks (e.g., see which functions have uncovered blocks).\n- clearer reports (packages distinguishable).\n\nCons:\n- changes artifact names/paths: build/<cfg>/t1_dist_matrix_c/main.exe → t1_dist_matrix_c.exe or t1_dist_matrix_с/main_c.exe.\n- `coverage.settings.xml` ModulePaths regex must change.\n- Any scripts/docs referencing `main.exe` (README, maybe e2e results naming, journal) — e2e uses TARGET_FILE so fine.\n- The course/AGENTS says outputs were deliberately named `main` (CMakeLists comment at line 271). Let me read that comment to see the rationale. If the rationale is \"single entry point / uniform path\", renaming breaks it.\n\nLet me read CMakeLists around 260-300 to see the comment.\n\nActually earlier grep showed:\n```\n271:  # 楫� � �� ��室���. 楫� ����� ���� ��� (�����᪮�, ⨯� t1_c), � ᤥ����� �� 䠩� - ��㣮� (OUTPUT_NAME main)\n276:  OUTPUT_NAME main\n```\nMojibake, but roughly: \"цель не по имени? цель может быть как ... (например, для t1_c), а сделать ее файлом - другой (OUTPUT_NAME main)\". Let me decode.\n\nLet me read it properly with cp1251.\n\nAlso: is block metric even needed for the deliverable? §4.7: \"отчёт с разбором непокрытых веток\". Since branch is unavailable, block is a proxy. We can get block info for common (via DLLs) but not for tasks. The 25 uncovered lines were found by line-level. Would block data reveal