erage.\n- **AGENTS §7 journal** — the dated run report: 589 tests, union 671/693, the table of remaining 22 lines with classification, the z_span fix (input, expected, verification), commands and outputs. Numbers live here because they change.\n- **CHANGELOG** — a line: added coverage stage (0.3.0? or Unreleased). Actually the user already has CHANGELOG with 0.2.0 released. Coverage stage → new version 0.3.0 or Unreleased. That's a separate decision (the journal mentions versioning rules). Mention briefly.\n- Why not a separate doc: project is small; README + journal is enough; a third place would duplicate.\n\nAlso: recommend NOT putting the full table in README because it goes stale; instead put the *method* and the *categories*, plus a pointer \"актуальный разбор — в журнале, дата X\".\n\nBut the course deliverable \"отчёт с разбором непокрытых веток\" — the mentor likely reads the journal anyway. So journal is the artifact.\n\nLet me also propose the exact subsection outline for README:\n```\n### Покрытие\n- как запустить (preset coverage + target)\n- артефакты: coverage.coverage / .cobertura.xml / .xml и что где\n- как читать: union vs root; атрибуция по путям; main-пакет\n- что считается результатом: line-level (branch у инструмента нет)\n```\nAnd in \"Известные ограничения\":\n- только Windows (MSVC); на Linux — gcov/будущий этап\n- branch-метрики нет; block есть, но по 8 задачам теряется из-за OUTPUT_NAME main\n- OOM-ветки не исполняются без инъекции\n- io-fail только на Linux\n- `LastTestsFailed.log` — последний непустой набор падений\n- `coverage` — отдельная сборка, не Debug/Release\n\nAlso mention where the run-specific numbers go and why.\n\nOne more: README is UTF-8; so edits must be UTF-8 (unlike expected headers CP1251). Worth flagging since the user carefully manages encodings — the README edit via normal tools is fine (Write/edit produce UTF-8), but the CP1251 files need the PowerShell approach.\n\nLet me answer concisely with the recommendation an