          "text": "Now verify:\n\n### README 68-69\n- 68: \"cmake скрипт для формирования отчётов .cobertura.xml, .xml. внутри себя запускает colletc, ctest; обеспечивает удаление старых отчётов в начале свежего coverage-build; при частичной инструментации или красных тестах падает только после формирования отчётов.\"\n  - Typo: \"colletc\" → \"collect\".\n  - \"запускает collect, ctest\" — technically collect launches ctest; the script launches collect which runs ctest. Fine as a simplification, but \"запускает collect, ctest\" reads as two parallel commands. Minor.\n  - \"при частичной инструментации ... падает только после формирования отчётов\" — is that accurate? Let's think: if instrumentation is partial but collect returns 0 (no test failures), the script does NOT fail — it just produces a report. The script fails only when `_collect_rc != 0`. So \"при частичной инструментации ... падает\" is **wrong**: partial instrumentation doesn't make collect return non-zero necessarily, and the script doesn't detect it. Partially instrumented modules appear in skipped_* and the report is produced silently. So the phrase overstates: the FATAL condition is non-zero collect rc, which we interpret as \"tests failed or collection failed\". Partial instrumentation is not detected.\n  \n  Actually — could partial instrumentation cause non-zero rc? Unclear. But the statement \"при частичной инструментации ... падает только после формирования отчётов\" implies the script detects partial instrumentation and fails. It doesn't. This should be corrected: \"если `collect` завершился с ненулевым кодом (красные тесты или сбой сбора) — отчёты всё равно формируются, и только потом падение. Частичная инструментация отдельно не детектируется: пропуски видны в native XML (`skipped_module`/`skipped_function`).\"\n\n  Hmm, but is it worth this much nuance in the structure section? It's a factual overstatement. Flag it.\n\n- 69: \"coverage.settings.xml - для фильтрации модулей: `common_*_shared.dll` и `tests/unit/*.exe`(т.к. там внутри статически зашит common); исключаются ... gtest/boost/vcpkg. и есть инструментация потомков ...\"\n  - Missing the task modules (`t[1-4]_*/main.exe`) in the inclusion list! The settings includes them. The sentence says \"для фильтрации модулей: common_*_shared.dll и tests/unit/*.exe\" — omits main.exe. That's an omission (previously the description said \"tests/\"; now it lists two of three includes). Should add \"модули задач (`t[1-4]_*/main.exe`)\".\n  - Also \"т.к. там внутри статически зашит common\" — for tests/unit exes: only some link common (parse_point/centroid/etc.), others link string_utils only. \"статические библиотеки common\" would be more accurate. Minor.\n  - Missing space before parenthesis: \"`tests/unit/*.exe`(т.к.\" — style.\n\n### CHANGELOG\n\nLine 7: \"сборка под coverage флагами, не противоречащими Microsoft.CodeCoverage.Console (/O2 /Ob1 /Zi, линкер /DEBUG - отличны и от build, и от release. потому и отдельная сборка)\" — grammatically broken: \"сборка под coverage флагами\" (missing \"с\"). Also \"отличны и от build, и от release\" — \"build\" presumably means Debug. Should be \"отличаются и от Debug, и от Release\". Also technically `/O2 /Ob1 /Zi` differ from Debug (/Od) and Release (/O2 /Ob2). Correct. And `/DEBUG` is present in Release too (per CMakeLists Release link flags include /DEBUG). Hmm: in `configure_target`, Release gets `/DEBUG /OPT:REF /OPT:ICF`; Coverage gets `/DEBUG` only. So the claim \"линкер /DEBUG ... отличны и от build, и от release\" is inaccurate: /DEBUG is in both Debug and Release. What's distinct: `/Ob1` (vs /Ob2 in Release), no /OPT flags, no ASan. So the parenthetical is partly wrong.\n  Suggest: \"сборка под coverage с флагами, совместимыми с Microsoft.CodeCoverage.Console (`/O2 /Ob1 /Zi`, линкер `/DEBUG`; отличается от Debug отсутствием ASan, от Release — `/Ob1` вместо `/Ob2` и без `/OPT:REF /OPT:ICF`)\".\n  \nLine 8: \"сделана проверка инструмента - наличия и версии ... (min 18.0, tested 18.7). min/max версии лежат константами...\" — \"min/max\" is wrong: the constants are MIN and TESTED, not MAX. [FACT] Should be \"min/tested\". Fix.\n\nLine 9: \"build-цель coverage - запустит скриптовый coverage.cmake, который соберёт всё (DEPENDS all), и запустит тесты того, что не исключено ... она же фигурирует в CMakePresets.json как пресет\" — Actually the *preset* is a configure preset; the *build target* is `coverage`. Saying \"она же фигурирует ... как пресет\" is imprecise: the preset `coverage` is a configure preset (CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Coverage), not the target. They're related but not the same. Fix: \"в CMakePresets.json есть пресет `coverage` (CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Coverage), а цель сборки — `cmake --build build/coverage --target coverage`\". \n  Also \"запустит тесты того, что не исключено\" — fine.\n\nLine 10: coverage.cmake description — correct.\nLine 11: \"два формата ... cobertura переносим, но имеет только line-rate; .xml имеет block-rate для модулей с уникальными именами и показывает partially-покрытие\" — accurate. Minor: \"partially-покрытие\" → \"частичное покрытие (covered=\\\"partial\\\")\". Fine.\nLine 12: \"coverage.settings.xml - для фильтрации отчёта и инструментации потомков collect\" — same imprecision as README but acceptable; could mention module list. Minor.\nLine 13: t3_z_span — correct. \"закрывает ветки min/max по y/z\" — actually it closes max.z, min.y, min.z (max.y was already covered). \"по y/z\" is a fair summary. ✓\nLine 14: \".gitignore добавлен *.coverage и *.cobertura.xml\" — verify. Earlier grep showed only `*.coverage` at line 8. Let me re-check .gitignore now — the user may have added both. Need to verify.\nLine 15: \".editorconfig к utf-8 группе прибавлен *.xml\" — verify .editorconfig. Let me check: coverage.settings.xml is XML with ASCII only, but adding *.xml to utf-8 is fine. Need to verify it was added.\n\nSo I should check .gitignore and .editorconfig.\n\nAlso format: Keep a Changelog order now Added first — good. No empty Changed. ✓\n\nUnreleased stays — per user's decision (version bump only after summary + OUTPUT_NAME + Linux). Good; just confirm.\n\nLet me check .gitignore and .editorconfig.",
